From cc98af0c89aef16402feb5c5dd4bbfb87af5d527 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:41:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use modern macOS content-type APIs in native GLib

The pinned GLib backend uses deprecated CoreServices UTI calls, which fail the native macOS build with -Werror=deprecated-declarations (hosted run 38813867936). Use UniformTypeIdentifiers with bounded autorelease pools and retained CFString results, preserving fallback behavior and self-conformance of undeclared types. Declare its exact system framework dependency in runtime projection. Add GIO worker-thread and framework relocation regressions.

Local source extraction, six source-preparation tests, maintained formatting, and the focused framework relocation regression pass. The framework regression fails before registration. Hosted run 38817369397 compiles the complete native prefix successfully and exposes the missing framework registration. Native runtime acceptance on the final emitted candidate remains required.
